{
  "format": "call-of-slop-construct-blueprint/1",
  "name": "Packet Spine Freighter",
  "description": "The Traders' spine freighter: a crew cab under a small glass cockpit, then a thin walkable spine with twelve open cargo racks strapped along its flanks, six a side, each holding two 8-foot cube containers one over the other, and an engineering block aft with a drive nacelle on a pylon to each side. The crew live in the cab: bunks, a head, a trade office, a galley, an airlock over the boarding shaft and the stores. Lift jets and legs under the cab and engineering set it down; attitude jets at both ends and on the nacelles' noses move it about. Its containers ride in frozen cargo volumes, one on each rack.",
